"ele366y" <ele366y@yahoo.com> wrote:

> A few experiments in Wizard mode are showing me
> that you can't really polymorph that many objects
> either in a line or in a pile.  I get four or five
> objects total, that's it.  What am I doing wrong
> here?

You can do both.

Make a line of small piles, four piles may be the
limit, I haven't done this for a long time. In
each pile, _mix_ the stuff you put in the pile. For
a golem to be created, there must be enough of its
source material in that particular pile, so if the
pile is a mix of scrolls, armor, glass, etc, then
no golem, within limits.

Zap down the line, check for goodies.

I'm moderately sure that both BUC status and any
enchantment are preserved, if possible (you can't
save the enchantment on a ring that changes to a
type, like slow digestion, that doesn't accept +1,
+2, etc.), so if you make "first pile blessed,
second pile uncursed, third pile cursed", or perhaps
"first pile +3, second pile +2, third pile +1" you
should be able to save some ID effort.  Test this
before trying it in a real game, though, like I
said, it's been a long time, and the game may have
changed or I may misremember.

Remember too, that polymorphing is lossy, so some of
the stuff you put in the piles may softly and quietly
vanish away, as if nabbed by a boojum.

